[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250321 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63035e67-c066-56f1-897a-8d319b27f7c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{6x+1}{4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248321} {:answer/id #uuid "728659a8-4d30-5f53-b783-77ca68417d8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{6x+1}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248426} {:answer/id #uuid "7c54a2d2-9684-516e-a49e-05b02d5d4c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{6x+1}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248517} {:answer/id #uuid "aaa8f858-6398-51a7-9ffc-de9e24072ba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{6x+1}{4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248942} {:answer/id #uuid "c56cf019-abf9-5371-bc50-d8f4dfad801e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{6x+1}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c54a2d2-9684-516e-a49e-05b02d5d4c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{6x+1}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248517} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa53ad0f-77f4-501c-a778-132511875487" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249972}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "efd4eb6a-b650-553c-bcc2-ab2b63a8dbe2" :question/math-academy-id "q-114918" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-{(6x+1)}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-(6x+1)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4(1-(6x+1)^{2}/4)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{1-(6x+1)^{2}/4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-(6x+1)^{2}/4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(6x+1)^{2}/4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((6x+1)/2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(\\frac{6x+1}{2}).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=\\frac{6x+1}{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-(6x+1)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((6x+1)/2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{6x+1}{2})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250322 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31c17a05-d2f9-5ba0-b754-dcbfc7f9b4eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x-3}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247879} {:answer/id #uuid "4ccaaf30-f65e-532d-85cd-8c1ce995b1fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\text{arcsec}(x-3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248111} {:answer/id #uuid "8f1dda95-180f-5a89-bfe9-5307962c3d37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(x-3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248697} {:answer/id #uuid "c56c203a-3635-5203-8a26-4d2596b69db1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(x-3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249180} {:answer/id #uuid "ec86287a-069c-51b9-9eb7-959c7a23a3fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(2(x-3))+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f1dda95-180f-5a89-bfe9-5307962c3d37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(x-3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248697} :answer-field/id #uuid "83644fa9-f278-5c29-b9fd-b62b8c892acc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249900}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d48157cd-3ea4-5a4b-b2a2-ea19ff6fa51b" :question/math-academy-id "q-114923" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{2}{|x-3|\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{|x-3|\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{|x-3|\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x-3).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=x-3.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{|x-3|\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{|x-3|\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\,\\text{arcsec}(u)+C \\\\  & =2\\,\\text{arcsec}(x-3)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250324 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "001d516e-ba06-5b95-b4a6-f35dab9a3672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(x+4)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247415} {:answer/id #uuid "14ed51ee-756e-57ce-98c5-e09580d0ea4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{arcsec}(x-4)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247613} {:answer/id #uuid "1d6dbd24-53a8-57ca-8ab3-2c785beb7617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(x-4)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247686} {:answer/id #uuid "3fd72e51-75ac-59c4-906c-a14dfbeed5aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x-4}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247990} {:answer/id #uuid "4deeee7d-3bfe-54f3-bb50-f18cec4519b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x+4}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d6dbd24-53a8-57ca-8ab3-2c785beb7617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(x-4)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247686} :answer-field/id #uuid "8347f822-40d4-57c9-9262-ff4fdf512681" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "07920739-bd19-5b4b-b343-8e19ac7c6d5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114928" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8x+15 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+({4}^{2}-{4}^{2})+15 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-8x+16)-16+15 \\\\  & =(x-4)^{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{(x-4)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $x-4.$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=x-4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{(x-4)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(x-4)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250325 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "069e5dc3-903f-56c3-80b2-a36d93cb6a14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(x-2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247483} {:answer/id #uuid "4ee8a822-9e03-5b0b-9157-4a6e261fd6ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{arcsec}(2(x+2))+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248134} {:answer/id #uuid "5c9b7170-e2cb-5afb-ae16-7aa25d17f2fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248268} {:answer/id #uuid "8c688811-e631-576f-b3af-fccf1d19453f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x+2}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248679} {:answer/id #uuid "c73082f2-4cbb-5c23-891d-47290806832d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x-2}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c9b7170-e2cb-5afb-ae16-7aa25d17f2fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248268} :answer-field/id #uuid "76fa23d1-4298-5709-9837-39a75683bfac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fd2cd352-82c1-595a-88b3-99447daccebc" :question/math-academy-id "q-114929" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4x+3 & ={x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+({2}^{2}-{2}^{2})+3 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+4x+4)-4+3 \\\\  & =(x+2)^{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{(x+2)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $x+2.$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=x+2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{(x+2)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(x+2)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250326 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01c50259-96ff-5091-b6d8-d010aabcd87a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{2}-3}{4{ln}^{2}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247435} {:answer/id #uuid "5b1b58be-7936-591f-a3c9-e22825f21d58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248249} {:answer/id #uuid "602d95a8-3c49-5628-a5fc-26ae6d4442af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248293} {:answer/id #uuid "ae45cdbd-b5db-5833-8170-fccfe8733b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{e}^{3}-2}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248981} {:answer/id #uuid "f16fc0ad-7654-55ab-873b-8984cf712d78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249543}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae45cdbd-b5db-5833-8170-fccfe8733b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{e}^{3}-2}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248981} :answer-field/id #uuid "46bceeef-1e66-56f1-87c4-0b40ebcc4c53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249799}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c7237523-38ec-5167-93d0-30747905ffb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-114942" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}9{x}^{2}({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2{log}_{2}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=9{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int 9{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=3{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 9{x}^{2}({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={({log}_{2}⁡x)}^{2}(3{x}^{3})-\\int (3{x}^{3})(\\frac{2{log}_{2}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}{({log}_{2}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate  $\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{2}⁡x)(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡x}{3}-\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡x}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 9{x}^{2}({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{x}^{3}{({log}_{2}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\frac{{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡x}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+D) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}{({log}_{2}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{3}{ln}^{2}⁡x}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}+\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3{ln}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2}{3})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{6D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$\n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}9{x}^{2}({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3{ln}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2}{3})]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3{ln}^{2}⁡e-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+\\frac{2}{3})-\\frac{{1}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3{ln}^{2}⁡1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3-2+\\frac{2}{3})-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(0-0+\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5{e}^{3}}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\frac{2}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5{e}^{3}-2}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250327 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f84bc89-0f5f-5174-b311-6b1ac207d432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4e-8}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248845} {:answer/id #uuid "acd12eca-de9b-50f1-ae82-10635e26c184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e-6}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248968} {:answer/id #uuid "f04115a5-6b2e-5bc2-9ed5-4e7dbb828a37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249532} {:answer/id #uuid "f2594c73-abaa-58dd-995b-af12abd8461c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249549} {:answer/id #uuid "f538ac92-7bb7-5776-a593-eda1db9ee897" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4e+3}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f84bc89-0f5f-5174-b311-6b1ac207d432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4e-8}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248845} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b1851a2-09ca-5e98-9283-451c4f3c0948" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ee94ab2f-1f66-5795-8930-e1ab98c8dab8" :question/math-academy-id "q-114944" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{4{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}-\\int (x)(\\frac{4{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}-\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int {log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate  $\\int {log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})-\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =x{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}-\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})-\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D) \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}-\\frac{4x{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{8x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}-\\frac{4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+\\frac{8x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}({ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+8)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{4D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{3}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$\n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}({ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+8)]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}({ln}^{2}⁡({e}^{2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})+8)-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}({ln}^{2}⁡({1}^{2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{2})+8) \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(4-8+8)-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(0-0+8) \\\\  & =\\frac{4e-8}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250328 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "101c128a-6dc8-5632-a7ae-f0b91b164739" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{e}^{5}+3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247565} {:answer/id #uuid "2adceece-a53a-577c-9b55-b2e47ed35eb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{5}-2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247806} {:answer/id #uuid "2c5aca5e-dc8e-5ba7-9af6-c2a386609510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247817} {:answer/id #uuid "a227ec20-ef2b-5e2e-b4e4-2aca175b50f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17{e}^{5}-2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248872} {:answer/id #uuid "dbbef6d4-187f-5f47-a784-698d678b5e58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{e}^{5}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a227ec20-ef2b-5e2e-b4e4-2aca175b50f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17{e}^{5}-2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248872} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a3c2387-20aa-5008-8cd7-6fc006779faf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d87d568c-f1e1-5dbc-b0f7-7053ed2197d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-114946" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}25{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2} & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=25{x}^{4} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 25{x}^{4}\\text{d}x=5{x}^{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 25{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}(5{x}^{5})-\\int (5{x}^{5})(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-10\\int {x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int {x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{4} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int {x}^{4}\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5})(\\frac{1}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}\\int {x}^{4}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{25}+D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 25{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\text{d}x & =5{x}^{5}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-10\\int {x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-10(\\frac{{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{25}+D) \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-2{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2{x}^{5}}{5}-10D \\\\  & ={x}^{5}(5{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2}{5})+C\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-10D.$ Finally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}25{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\text{d}x & ={[{x}^{5}(5{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2}{5})]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =[{e}^{5}(5{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e)}^{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+\\frac{2}{5})]-[{1}^{5}(5{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)}^{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+\\frac{2}{5})] \\\\  & =[{e}^{5}(5-2+\\frac{2}{5})]-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{17{e}^{5}-2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250330 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21fa41e6-4e3a-5806-859d-c2aaa4b58edc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247725} {:answer/id #uuid "3aad9910-8581-517c-bee6-27e599bcdafd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247943} {:answer/id #uuid "81ff4d92-1a10-5646-988f-1c901a51022f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248576} {:answer/id #uuid "9f6e5a27-6ad8-5b1a-b327-7847f10b1222" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248844} {:answer/id #uuid "cefcf51a-b70a-5c3a-a3be-b1a5d98e9adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81ff4d92-1a10-5646-988f-1c901a51022f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248576} :answer-field/id #uuid "6117be46-83ef-580f-84ce-56c76fa2d084" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f09819e-da12-5415-9b7c-4388f9ed375d" :question/math-academy-id "q-114952" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x$ using integration by parts." :question/worked-solution "First, we let\n\n$$\nI=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{2}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{4x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{2}⁡x(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4})(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4}-2\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4}-2I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $I,$ remembering to add a constant of integration $C$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4}-2I \\\\ 3I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{12}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250331 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "522547ac-6535-5fb0-b8a3-a2053a87b01d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248161} {:answer/id #uuid "5dffb7ca-1a66-52ae-b04f-97ae522f8f3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248279} {:answer/id #uuid "751980ea-1704-5381-ae28-6aa05cfad2e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248453} {:answer/id #uuid "90fe0781-abfd-56c8-9147-cf8bdbde8121" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248713} {:answer/id #uuid "9d475fa0-a4da-59e4-b41c-47c13378b87f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "751980ea-1704-5381-ae28-6aa05cfad2e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248453} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0704fd5-1897-52d9-acd5-2f3d7565c6ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250031}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "85a3e0f2-59ad-5501-8562-0840b6094216" :question/math-academy-id "q-114965" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x$ using integration by parts." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{6}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{6{ln}^{5}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{6}⁡x)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)(\\frac{6{ln}^{5}⁡x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{7}⁡x-6\\int \\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{7}⁡x-6I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $I.$ We can ignore the constant of integration in this case, because it is insignificant for further evaluation of the definite integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={ln}^{7}⁡x-6I \\\\ 7I & ={ln}^{7}⁡x \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{7}⁡x}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}({ln}^{7}⁡x){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}({ln}^{7}⁡(e)-{ln}^{7}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250332 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c0432af-5e36-5fda-8917-32b349683fe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247816} {:answer/id #uuid "38592cbc-383b-5e42-b2c1-16c799f4dac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247927} {:answer/id #uuid "472b2169-b73e-52b2-a759-79ee2c0017dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248056} {:answer/id #uuid "a124094c-2198-56e3-a44a-8e218a714881" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248864} {:answer/id #uuid "c2c76c8f-f2d8-5896-8bd2-98aa7de77cc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{40}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2c76c8f-f2d8-5896-8bd2-98aa7de77cc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{40}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249157} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfceba82-e7c8-58e8-a6e1-6dbed0dd06ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aafbcc52-b05c-5248-b40a-c0ce083a128b" :question/math-academy-id "q-114999" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x$ using integration by parts." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{9}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{9{ln}^{8}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{4x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{9}⁡x)(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4})(\\frac{9{ln}^{8}⁡x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{4}-9\\int \\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{4}-9I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $I.$ We can ignore the constant of integration in this case, because it is insignificant for further evaluation of the definite integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{4}-9I \\\\ 10I & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{4} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{40}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{40}({ln}^{10}⁡x){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{40}({ln}^{10}⁡(e)-{ln}^{10}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{40}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250359 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "018d8348-3190-5eea-b417-c63541e4aff5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247430} {:answer/id #uuid "08eab5fa-3385-5df5-b8fd-2f29432c498e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247499} {:answer/id #uuid "1eb0449b-6ed5-5ab7-9e17-f2f9074c0612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247696} {:answer/id #uuid "2e1524c0-3b53-58d5-b338-ecb0ead5ac3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247832} {:answer/id #uuid "67f62f68-93fb-55cb-a9ad-f01fff119dc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "018d8348-3190-5eea-b417-c63541e4aff5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247430} :answer-field/id #uuid "078894b3-54fc-5c41-9c56-f018aef4c9b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9725f40a-ccc5-5b84-9193-a09e8482b8d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-115218" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\frac{1}{3}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x+1}\\le \\frac{1}{9}.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x+1} & \\le \\frac{1}{9} \\\\ {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x+1} & \\le \\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡[{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x+1}] & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ (x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}) & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ (x+1)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ (x+1)(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & \\le -\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, note that $-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ is a negative quantity, so when we divide both sides by it, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & \\ge \\frac{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ x & \\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250360 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "302b378f-be12-5ba0-97fd-06dd7fe61909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le -6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247858} {:answer/id #uuid "3173ff57-51bd-5dc4-8c31-633792b6a1b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{4}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247872} {:answer/id #uuid "433231b9-72f8-5a2a-b270-d72099dbaf75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{4}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248027} {:answer/id #uuid "cb82884c-5f42-579d-a3b2-766dcd5e9b0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249235} {:answer/id #uuid "f6af4d9b-c12c-51d1-a663-b88288cd8554" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "302b378f-be12-5ba0-97fd-06dd7fe61909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le -6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247858} :answer-field/id #uuid "759dac82-e131-5166-b8ec-519724d4e077" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ac4b46ad-428b-596b-a6dd-aa26aa057694" :question/math-academy-id "q-115222" :question/problem "Solve the inequality ${(\\frac{3}{4})}^{x+6}+1\\ge 2.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{x+6}+1 & \\ge 2 \\\\ {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{x+6} & \\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡[{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{x+6}] & \\ge \\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\ (x+6)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{4}) & \\ge 0 \\\\ (x+6)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) & \\ge 0 \\\\ (x+6)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, note that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ is a negative quantity, so when we divide both sides by it, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+6) & \\le \\frac{0}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ x+6 & \\le 0 \\\\ x & \\le -6\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250365 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bddbba4-895d-5993-b7ec-55a01d328fa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247530} {:answer/id #uuid "50e8f068-fe0e-581f-8ae4-9a985a1bdef5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248151} {:answer/id #uuid "52bdc298-cd04-5aaf-a6fa-fcf496dbdd22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248169} {:answer/id #uuid "6c791cdd-bf14-5cdc-a55a-2374ab3e0790" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "all real numbers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248383} {:answer/id #uuid "78b2b35b-752c-54d4-a1db-65d499c76704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{6}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50e8f068-fe0e-581f-8ae4-9a985a1bdef5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248151} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bdff120-3f6b-5674-abcd-9423a762d861" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249717}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ef8ebb72-c9f4-522b-b5c8-2cd601e5dcba" :question/math-academy-id "q-115233" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $2{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2x+7}+1<-5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the exponential term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2x+7}+1 & <-5 \\\\ 2{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2x+7} & <-6 \\\\ {(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2x+7} & <-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, recall that a positive number raised to any real power is always positive. Since $\\frac{1}{3}>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2x+7}>0\n$$\n\nfor every real value of $x.$\n\nTherefore, ${(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2x+7}$ cannot be less than $-3.$ Hence, the inequality\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2x+7}<-3\n$$\n\nhas no solutions."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250370 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e749b95-3859-5caf-bfd8-c834793e8ed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247694} {:answer/id #uuid "40bebdef-ae8a-5d9e-ac28-6228e738db2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247995} {:answer/id #uuid "49f23bbb-2f76-5966-bbae-3c9d22acc9ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248082} {:answer/id #uuid "b99ff983-b6ef-5e58-8aa0-af927de0b3fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249083} {:answer/id #uuid "f6b0c71b-a6be-59ae-b32b-dde21ce862fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49f23bbb-2f76-5966-bbae-3c9d22acc9ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248082} :answer-field/id #uuid "7730106b-6087-572a-9b32-b26564608b47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249875}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c08f0a1-4fee-59ab-b31f-f6a9816dc7a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-115250" :question/problem "Solve the inequality ${5}^{x-1}<{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2-x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{x-1} & <{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2-x} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{x-1}) & <\\operatorname{ln}⁡[{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2-x}] \\\\ (x-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & <(2-x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ (x-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & <(2-x)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\ (x-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & <(2-x)(0-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\ (x-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & <(x-2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & <x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & <\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & <\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ x & <\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250397 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e785456-0d46-526f-9e67-18d57eadc06a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247557} {:answer/id #uuid "2a9b3b46-47ed-564d-81ee-53957c02a43a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247803} {:answer/id #uuid "5dbce6e1-d015-5841-ac53-b3bc03022688" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{2}{x-2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248277} {:answer/id #uuid "cecf1feb-5477-5f51-924d-678fd3092009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{4}{x-2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249257} {:answer/id #uuid "d4bba209-bdae-5fcc-b9cd-f07175cf1210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-\\frac{4}{x-2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dbce6e1-d015-5841-ac53-b3bc03022688" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{2}{x-2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248277} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a5dba1e-963f-540d-840f-945c1bcdcb43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249807}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "804e099a-7eac-522b-b475-41496ab8d992" :question/math-academy-id "q-115323" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{4x-10}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4x-10}{(x-2)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{(x-2)}+\\frac{B}{(x-2)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-2)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n4x-10=A(x-2)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2)-10 & =A(2-2)+B \\\\ -2 & =0+B \\\\ B & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(0)-10 & =A(0-2)+B \\\\ -10 & =-2A-2 \\\\ -2A & =-8 \\\\ A & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\frac{4x-10}{(x-2)^{2}}=\\frac{4}{(x-2)}-\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4x-10}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{4}{(x-2)}-\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int \\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-2(-\\frac{1}{x-2})+C \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{2}{x-2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250404 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a329a54-4f81-5bc7-9972-9d32effaa6c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{1}{3}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248241} {:answer/id #uuid "ac7e6dcd-4341-5ca3-9e25-273a9f542d85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-9y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248963} {:answer/id #uuid "b68ce2f4-36aa-5333-97d7-e92257913ac5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{9}{4}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249059} {:answer/id #uuid "d9433e5e-716b-5504-ac6b-94eed855c88e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=9y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249342} {:answer/id #uuid "e443c042-27a8-5be0-ac68-ea847b0c1a54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=3y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9433e5e-716b-5504-ac6b-94eed855c88e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=9y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249342} :answer-field/id #uuid "11e01a2f-c7f0-58e1-95b2-bb107a5aa3e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249701}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0dfebbb3-1e7f-58e9-a0ac-939acd360f4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-115415" :question/problem "![](images/52/52b283fd5a8d9f374fad0a007f127598b86c53d7acf4df05d1415589e43faaa0.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the parabola is upward-opening, has its vertex at $(0,0),$ and passes through the point $(3,1).$\n\nFor any upward or downward-opening parabola whose vertex is $(0,0),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe know that the given parabola passes through the point $(3,1),$ so we can substitute $x=3$ and $y=1$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {3}^{2} & =4p(1) \\\\ 9 & =4p \\\\ p & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(\\frac{9}{4})y \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250405 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04ffa276-379e-5b1f-ade7-d6d1a255f79b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{5}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247460} {:answer/id #uuid "213191af-0b1c-54df-85c1-bfc33aa407a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{25}{8}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247717} {:answer/id #uuid "367a9704-d0cd-52a6-8c9e-1f43b931615b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{25}{2}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247915} {:answer/id #uuid "75227f58-c686-5197-87a0-5b1edfb5b5f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{2}{25}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248454} {:answer/id #uuid "c5048ebb-d0b2-50a9-9408-f2aac2c86149" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{4}{5}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "367a9704-d0cd-52a6-8c9e-1f43b931615b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{25}{2}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247915} :answer-field/id #uuid "8461e255-e863-501e-bc4f-d4c3f00fa748" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249901}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "913fe829-246c-5859-8570-cf82a68a6df8" :question/math-academy-id "q-115420" :question/problem "![](images/41/410da7fdbf283aba57c2000a37c56a87e11ed1b1372183a1d3c808376dba495f.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the parabola is upward-opening, has its vertex at $(0,0),$ and passes through the point $(-5,2).$\n\nFor any upward or downward-opening parabola whose vertex is $(0,0),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe know that the given parabola passes through the point $(-5,2),$ so we can substitute $x=-5$ and $y=2$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ (-5)^{2} & =4p(2) \\\\ 25 & =8p \\\\ p & =\\frac{25}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(\\frac{25}{8})y \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{2}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250411 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "094e6092-339d-5805-b65a-0ba9ea32fcb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{4}{5}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247504} {:answer/id #uuid "14563ff8-ab85-58f1-81f8-f36ec51e3961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{25}{8}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247607} {:answer/id #uuid "469c754e-d524-520c-ab78-58d1d9ef15b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{5}{2}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248054} {:answer